on-arrival: right_spd_r_saxony = aspd_r_saxony; aspd_name = "ASPD"; heldt_in = aspd_name; buck_in = aspd_name; ebert_in = aspd_name if ebert_in = "I"; workers_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 2; new_middle_spd -= 2; old_middle_spd -= 1; rural_spd -= 1; aspd_relation = 50 if ideology == "reformist"; aspd_relation = 40 if ideology == "labor"; aspd_relation = 40 if ideology == "centrist"; aspd_relation = 20 if ideology == "left"; aspd_leader = "Buck"; aspd_ideology = "Social Democratic Pragmatism"; wor_aspd_s = 0.6; un_aspd_s = 0.6; new_aspd = 0.2
new-page: true

= New Social Democratic Party in Saxony

With the reformists in the Saxon Parliament expelled from the <span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">**SPD**</span> they have decided to form their own party to compete with us and maintain their mandates. Since they claim to return to an older kind of less radical Social Democracy that focuses on making actual improvements for the people without ideological banter, the name they will carry is going to be <span style="color: [+ aspd_colour +];">**ASPD**</span> (Old Social-Democratic Party of Germany).

[? if ebert_in == "ASPD": President Ebert, despite not living in Saxony, immediately joined this new party that precisely reflects his personal and political values. His membership might open the door to further popularity accross the Reich. ?]

[? if reformist_dissent >= 45: Many reformists in our own party have expressed large-scale sympathies for this party, some are even openly considering to join if they keep getting treated the way the are in the <span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">**SPD**</span>. ?]















